{"authored" [{"question" "q-114681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{5x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x]}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot [0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{10}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{3x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)={cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348719" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}⁡4x-{cos}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x={cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}⁡4x-{cos}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{{\\int}} \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin {2\\theta} =2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin(2\\theta) = \\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}.\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta= \\dfrac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin \\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{x}{2} \\right) &= \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos\\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin x\t&= \\sin \\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos  \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right).\n  }\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( - \\cos {x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta -\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos 2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x = \\cos 6x,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\cos 6x\\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{6}\\sin6x+ C.\\\n                                                                \n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\cos^2 x  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\cos^2{x}$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} =2\\cos^2 x -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\cos^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\int ( \\cos {2x} +1) \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n                                                                 &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} +x\\right) + C\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{4}\\sin {2x} +\\dfrac{1}{2}x + C.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin^2(3x)  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-483.json" "file_sha256" "d4589f3407741b43cf9c39629536db1e81b0616e2a68d55c923258253899d4ab" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\sin^2$ term: \n\n$$\n\\cos {2\\theta}=1-2\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {2\\theta} \\right )=\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {6x} \\right )=\\sin^2(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-483.json" "file_sha256" "d4589f3407741b43cf9c39629536db1e81b0616e2a68d55c923258253899d4ab" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/assets/b9a4695c6e43ee5ceb15ea1bbb3ee1815fdbd87e9c8b4a4e8eeba1089750ff79.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cdf3b096f6c85db5dc278d862a4ca6c8b73e3a38dc02891eb5ec955ebfe6b82" "basis" 1196 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+17x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+\\frac{3}{2}(0)^{2}+17\\cdot 0]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )+\\frac{3}{2}{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+17(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =[0+0+0]-[0+\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}-\\frac{17\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =[0+\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cdf3b096f6c85db5dc278d862a4ca6c8b73e3a38dc02891eb5ec955ebfe6b82" "basis" 1196 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96b3c950dde71577c2afac8d52c6a48bf7dc78542d6bc2bc6a74fa9e2099e0bc" "basis" 1196 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cdf3b096f6c85db5dc278d862a4ca6c8b73e3a38dc02891eb5ec955ebfe6b82" "basis" 1196 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-74398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-74398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nRearranging the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-74398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-74398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-74398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-74398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/41304b7f8cbaf3df778e0f079a1651d2846f94dc74012db3b2ce936144eac8c7.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-10440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-10440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-10440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-10440" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-10440" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-10440" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{5x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x]}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot [0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{10}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{10}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/a2ccde221d71e611f7917d6dac0d12ca6b8204d9cd80a21d79005195245cf77a.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-348716" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348716" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})={cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})\\,{|}_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-348723" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348723" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/b9a4695c6e43ee5ceb15ea1bbb3ee1815fdbd87e9c8b4a4e8eeba1089750ff79.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+17x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+\\frac{3}{2}(0)^{2}+17\\cdot 0]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )+\\frac{3}{2}{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+17(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =[0+0+0]-[0+\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}-\\frac{17\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =[0+\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{17\\pi}{2}-\\frac{3\\pi^2}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}⁡4x-{cos}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x={cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}⁡4x-{cos}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{3x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)={cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-348719" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348719" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/f8aa97ff1ff27ec11df6aefd4523ed9d39efac686c777f7242701aa2f4fef79c.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+2-x]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3-x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+3x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+3(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}] \\\\  & =[\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-[0] \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pi -{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi^2}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 4{cos}^{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\theta =x$ and substituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{cos}^{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {(2{cos}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the same formula $2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1$ with $\\theta =2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\frac{3}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+\\frac{3}{2}\\,x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-114696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5{sin}^{2}⁡x+11{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{sin}^{2}⁡x+11{cos}^{2}⁡x & =5{sin}^{2}⁡x+5{cos}^{2}⁡x+6{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =5({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+6{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =5+6{cos}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5+6{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[5+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(8+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(8x+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})]-[8(0)+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(0))] \\\\  & =[4\\pi +\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )]-[0+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[4\\pi +\\frac{3}{2}(0)]-[0+\\frac{3}{2}(0)] \\\\  & =4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\pi )+\\pi -\\frac{1}{3}{\\pi }^{3})-(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+0-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi -{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3-{\\pi }^{2})}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi-\\frac{\\pi^3}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-347179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/b163cd4cc1add41ae2c043b4b3d7d818dd9b23de0a4b762bc85d348c0bca4def.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\pi $ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-347179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x+({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2x)\\,|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot (-\\pi ))+2(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =(0+\\pi )-(0-2\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\pi +2\\pi  \\\\  & =3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-347179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-347179" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-347179" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/d1d49c23cebfe2979c8bff7b7f19d5435807a8d1aec348070aadfab1e9d2ca19.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡(x),$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1)=-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7\\pi^3}{24}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348917" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/07a1fab6073fdff2a20140719b570c0c40981ab049866480fbaff4dfad0c7799.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x),$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$, as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348917" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ is \n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))={sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}{(x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x))|}_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}[(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi ))-(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348917" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-348917" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348917" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7\\pi}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (4{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (2\\cdot 2{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x-2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+6(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+C \\\\  & =2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3{x}^{2}+C \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-114706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{x}^{2}+x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "-{x}^{2}-4x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "3{x}^{2}-2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "{x}^{2}-x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int [1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "x-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(8{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{5}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(8{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(4[1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})]+4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(4-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})+4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(4x-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})+2{x}^{2})|}_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[4\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{2}-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2(5\\pi /2)}{5})+2{(\\frac{5\\pi }{2})}^{2}] \\\\  & \\,-[4\\cdot (-\\frac{5\\pi }{2})-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2(-5\\pi /2)}{5})+2{(-\\frac{5\\pi }{2})}^{2}] \\\\  & =[10\\pi -10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+2(\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{4})]-[-10\\pi -10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )+2(\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{4})] \\\\  & =[10\\pi -0+\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{2}]-[-10\\pi -0+\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{2}] \\\\  & =20\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb"} {"question" "q-348845" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "q-348845" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebab4b18f04cbd23bada016081f15ccf44e14bee6161175bf281abc7e8a52b15"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{{\\int}} \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin {2\\theta} =2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin(2\\theta) = \\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}.\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta= \\dfrac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin \\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{x}{2} \\right) &= \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos\\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin x\t&= \\sin \\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos  \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right).\n  }\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( - \\cos {x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta -\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos 2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x = \\cos 6x,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\cos 6x\\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{6}\\sin6x+ C.\\\n                                                                \n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\cos^2 x  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\cos^2{x}$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} =2\\cos^2 x -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\cos^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\int ( \\cos {2x} +1) \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n                                                                 &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} +x\\right) + C\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{4}\\sin {2x} +\\dfrac{1}{2}x + C.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin^2(3x)  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-483.json" "file_sha256" "d4589f3407741b43cf9c39629536db1e81b0616e2a68d55c923258253899d4ab"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\sin^2$ term: \n\n$$\n\\cos {2\\theta}=1-2\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {2\\theta} \\right )=\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {6x} \\right )=\\sin^2(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-483.j